"""Self-contained report, no CDN, tracking, or network calls."""
import json
from html import escape


def render(summaries, daily, manifest):
    payload = json.dumps(dict(summaries=summaries, daily=daily, manifest=manifest)).replace('<', '\\u003c')
    return '''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Inventory Decision Lab · Synthetic benchmark</title>
<style>
:root{--ink:#142c3a;--muted:#58707c;--paper:#f3f6f3;--teal:#167b73;--line:#d6e1dd}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}header{background:#132f3a;color:white;padding:42px max(5%,calc((100% - 1200px)/2)) 40px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,56px);line-height:1.08;margin:14px 0}h2{font-size:22px;margin:0 0 15px}h3{margin:0 0 8px}.eyebrow{color:#8ce0c6;font:12px monospace;letter-spacing:2px}header p{max-width:700px;color:#ccdeda}.wrap{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:28px 24px 60px}.banner{border-left:4px solid #bb8100;background:#fff4d7;padding:15px 20px;margin-bottom:25px}.controls{display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin:20px 0}select,input{font:inherit;padding:7px;border:1px solid #aec1ba;border-radius:6px}input{width:88px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px}.card,section{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin-bottom:20px}.metric{font-size:34px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1px}.small{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}.tag{color:var(--teal);font:12px monospace;text-transform:uppercase}.split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:20px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:12px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:right}td:first-child,th:first-child{text-align:left}.table-scroll{overflow:auto}button{background:var(--teal);border:0;color:white;border-radius:7px;padding:10px 14px;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}svg{width:100%;height:auto}a{color:var(--teal)}.note{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}#recommendation{font-size:19px}.legend{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:12px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px;max-height:300px;overflow:auto}@media(max-width:800px){.grid,.split{grid-template-columns:1fr}header{padding:28px 24px}.wrap{padding:20px 16px}.metric{font-size:28px}}
</style><header><div class="eyebrow">OPERATIONS / WORKING CAPITAL / DECISION SCIENCE</div><h1>Inventory Decision Lab</h1><p>How much service does inventory buy? Compare three replenishment policies against the same demand, supplier timing, and purchasing constraints.</p></header>
<main class="wrap"><div class="banner"><strong>Simulation, not achieved savings.</strong> All SKUs, demand, supplier terms, and costs are synthetic. Results are conditional on the displayed assumptions. This small-scenario walkthrough is not deployment approval; consult the separate held-out experiment.</div>
<div class="controls"><label>Scenario seed <select id="seed"><option value="all">All seeds (mean)</option></select></label><label>Service target <input id="target" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="95"> %</label><button id="download">Export displayed comparison</button></div>
<div class="grid" id="cards"></div>
<section><div class="tag">Illustrative scenario gate</div><p id="recommendation" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="note">Choose the lowest mean modeled cost among policies meeting the target in every selected seed. Changing the target filters these precomputed results; it does not rerun or tune the simulator. No feasible policy is a useful result.</p></section>
<div class="split"><section><h2>Service–cost trade-off</h2><div id="frontier"></div><p class="note">Lower cost and higher fill rate are preferable. Axes show observed ranges, not zero. Cost includes assumed shortage penalties, not measured profit.</p></section><section><h2>Daily closing inventory</h2><div id="trend"></div><div class="legend" id="legend"></div><p class="note">Units across the warehouse, averaged across selected seeds. A daily purchasing allowance resets each day; unused funds do not roll over.</p></section></div>
<section><h2>Policy comparison</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Policy</th><th>Fill rate</th><th>Modeled cost</th><th>Mean units / SKU</th><th>Orders</th><th>Constrained reviews</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table></div><p class="note">All policies share training-only initial stock, review days, allocation priority, and exogenous demand. Mean metrics across seeds are descriptive; no real-world confidence claim is made.</p></section>
<div class="split"><section><h2>What the model knows</h2><ul><li>56 days of training history by default; decisions use only observations available through that day.</li><li>Unmet demand is observed and lost permanently, with no backorders or substitution.</li><li>Supplier lead times are known and deterministic. Arrivals occur before daily demand; orders are placed afterward.</li><li>Scarce budget goes first to SKUs with the lowest inventory-position coverage, using a frozen training rate.</li></ul></section><section><h2>What to validate next</h2><ol><li>Measure actual lost demand, unit costs, supplier delays, and order minimums.</li><li>Agree on a service target and a defensible shortage penalty.</li><li>Run lead-time and budget stress scenarios; retain cases where every policy fails.</li><li>Pilot prospectively before claiming operating savings.</li></ol></section></div>
<section><h2>Audit trail & assumptions</h2><p id="assumptions"></p><p class="note">Ending inventory and paid in-transit orders remain assets with no terminal salvage credit. Acquisition spend is reported separately and excluded from the modeled operating-cost objective. Daily procurement cash caps include order fees; this is not a full cash-flow or profit model. Initial stock is endowed equally and not charged to the purchasing budget.</p><details><summary>Reproducible run manifest</summary><pre id="manifest"></pre></details></section>
<footer class="note">Original Python + SQLite experiment · Offline-first · MIT code / CC0 generated toy data</footer></main>
<script id="data" type="application/json">''' + payload + '''</script><script>
const D=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('data').textContent),names={fixed_periodic:'Fixed periodic',rolling_mean:'Rolling mean',seasonal_buffer:'Seasonal + buffer'},colors=['#167b73','#c26d35','#4960a5'],policies=Object.keys(names),$=id=>document.getElementById(id),money=x=>new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD',maximumFractionDigits:0}).format(x);
[...new Set(D.summaries.map(x=>x.seed))].forEach(s=>{let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=s;o.textContent=s;$('seed').append(o)});$('target').value=D.manifest.configs[0].service_target*100;
let shown=[];function render(){let ss=D.summaries.filter(x=>$('seed').value==='all'||x.seed==$('seed').value);shown=policies.map(p=>{let a=ss.filter(x=>x.policy===p),r={policy:p};Object.keys(a[0]).filter(k=>!['policy','seed'].includes(k)).forEach(k=>{let valid=a.filter(x=>x[k]!==null);r[k]=valid.length?valid.reduce((s,x)=>s+x[k],0)/valid.length:null});r.validFill=a.filter(x=>x.fill_rate!==null).length;r.undefinedFill=a.length-r.validFill;r.minFill=Math.min(...a.map(x=>x.fill_rate===null?-1:x.fill_rate));return r});let target=Number($('target').value)/100;let valid=String($('target').value).trim()!==''&&Number.isFinite(target)&&target>=0&&target<=1;let feasible=shown.filter(x=>valid&&x.minFill>=target).sort((a,b)=>a.modeled_cost_dollars-b.modeled_cost_dollars);let best=feasible[0];$('recommendation').textContent=!valid?'Enter a target between 0 and 100%.':best?names[best.policy]+' is the lowest-cost feasible policy for this selection. '+money(best.modeled_cost_dollars)+' mean modeled cost; '+(best.fill_rate*100).toFixed(1)+'% mean unit fill.':'No policy meets this service target in every selected seed. Revisit budget, review cadence, lead time, or the target before recommending an order policy.';
$('cards').innerHTML=shown.map((r,i)=>'<div class="card"><div class="tag">'+names[r.policy]+'</div><div class="metric">'+(r.fill_rate===null?'N/A':(r.fill_rate*100).toFixed(1)+'%')+'</div><div class="small">Unit fill rate · '+money(r.modeled_cost_dollars)+' modeled cost · '+r.validFill+' valid / '+r.undefinedFill+' undefined service seeds</div></div>').join('');
$('rows').innerHTML=shown.map(r=>'<tr><td>'+names[r.policy]+'</td><td>'+(r.fill_rate===null?'N/A':(100*r.fill_rate).toFixed(2)+'%')+'</td><td>'+money(r.modeled_cost_dollars)+'</td><td>'+r.mean_units_per_sku.toFixed(1)+'</td><td>'+r.orders.toFixed(0)+'</td><td>'+r.constrained_sku_reviews.toFixed(0)+'</td></tr>').join('');
let costs=shown.map(r=>r.modeled_cost_dollars),lo=Math.min(...costs)*.9,hi=Math.max(...costs)*1.1+1,fills=shown.filter(r=>r.fill_rate!==null).map(r=>r.fill_rate),fl=fills.length?Math.max(0,Math.min(...fills)-.04):0,fh=1;let dots=shown.filter(r=>r.fill_rate!==null).map(r=>{let i=policies.indexOf(r.policy),x=70+(r.modeled_cost_dollars-lo)/(hi-lo)*380,y=205-(r.fill_rate-fl)/(fh-fl||1)*160;return '<circle cx="'+x+'" cy="'+y+'" r="9" fill="'+colors[i]+'"><title>'+names[r.policy]+'</title></circle><text x="'+Math.min(x+12,345)+'" y="'+(y-12)+'" font-size="11">'+names[r.policy]+'</text>'}).join('');$('frontier').innerHTML='<svg viewBox="0 0 510 255" role="img" aria-label="Policy cost versus fill rate"><path d="M70 35V210H470" fill="none" stroke="#98ada4"/><text x="12" y="40" font-size="12">100%</text><text x="12" y="210" font-size="12">'+(fl*100).toFixed(0)+'%</text><text x="60" y="240" font-size="12">'+money(lo)+'</text><text x="395" y="240" font-size="12">'+money(hi)+'</text>'+dots+'</svg>';
let dd=D.daily.filter(x=>$('seed').value==='all'||x.seed==$('seed').value),series=policies.map(p=>{let m={};dd.filter(x=>x.policy===p).forEach(x=>{m[x.day]??=[];m[x.day].push(x.units)});return Object.keys(m).map(day=>({day:+day,units:m[day].reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/m[day].length}))}),max=Math.max(1,...series.flat().map(x=>x.units)),last=Math.max(1,...series.flat().map(x=>x.day));$('trend').innerHTML='<svg viewBox="0 0 510 255" role="img" aria-label="Daily total closing inventory"><path d="M55 30V215H485" fill="none" stroke="#98ada4"/>'+series.map((a,i)=>'<polyline fill="none" stroke="'+colors[i]+'" stroke-width="1.7" points="'+a.map(r=>(55+r.day/last*430)+','+(215-r.units/max*175)).join(' ')+'"/>').join('')+'<text x="5" y="43" font-size="12">'+max.toFixed(0)+'</text><text x="25" y="215" font-size="12">0</text><text x="55" y="240" font-size="12">Day 0</text><text x="430" y="240" font-size="12">Day '+last+'</text></svg>';
$('legend').innerHTML=policies.map((p,i)=>'<span style="color:'+colors[i]+'">● '+names[p]+'</span>').join('');}
$('seed').onchange=render;$('target').oninput=render;$('download').onclick=()=>{let keys=['policy','fill_rate','modeled_cost_dollars','mean_units_per_sku','orders','constrained_sku_reviews'],csv=[keys.join(','),...shown.map(r=>keys.map(k=>r[k]??'').join(','))].join('\\n'),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([csv],{type:'text/csv'}));a.download='simulated-policy-comparison.csv';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href),1000)};
let c=D.manifest.configs[0];$('assumptions').textContent=c.skus+' SKUs · '+c.days+' evaluation days · '+c.warmup+' training days · '+D.manifest.configs.length+' independent seeds · lead time '+c.lead_days+'–'+(c.lead_days+2)+' days · review every '+c.review_days+' days · daily procurement allowance '+money(c.daily_budget_cents/100)+' · shortage penalty '+money(c.shortage_cents/100)+'/unit';$('manifest').textContent=JSON.stringify(D.manifest,null,2);render();
</script></html>'''


def render_experiments(summary, selection, plan):
    data=json.dumps(dict(summary=summary,selected=selection,plan=plan)).replace('<','\\u003c')
    return '''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Decision Lab · Held-out evidence</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#eef3f0;color:#18343c;font:16px/1.5 system-ui}header{background:#15343d;color:#fff;padding:40px max(24px,calc((100vw - 1150px)/2))}h1{font-size:42px;line-height:1.1;margin:14px 0}header p{max-width:760px;color:#c3d8d3}.wrap{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:24px}.panel{padding:24px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d5e1dc;border-radius:12px;margin:20px 0}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px}.card{padding:22px;background:white;border:1px solid #d5e1dc;border-radius:12px}.big{font-size:32px;font-weight:700}.small{font-size:13px;color:#526e73}select{font:inherit;padding:9px;margin-left:12px;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #9cb4aa}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:12px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #e1e9e4;text-align:right}td:first-child,th:first-child{text-align:left}.scroll{overflow:auto}.notice{background:#fff1c7;padding:16px;border-left:4px solid #b67d1b}svg{width:100%;min-width:900px}.tag{font:12px monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:#167b73}header .tag{color:#94e8cd}details{margin-top:18px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px;max-height:400px;overflow:auto}button{font:inherit;background:#167b73;color:white;border:0;padding:10px 14px;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:760px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:32px}.wrap{padding:14px}}</style>
<header><div class="tag">Inventory Decision Lab / held-out experiment</div><h1>Does the decision survive stress?</h1><p>Separate policy selection from evaluation. Compare paired demand paths, show conditional uncertainty, and retain failure cases.</p></header><main class="wrap"><div class="notice">Synthetic simulation. Intervals measure variation across generated demand seeds, conditional on the model. They do not demonstrate real-world savings or validate the assumed cost model.</div><section class="panel"><div class="tag">Frozen decision</div><h2 id="decision"></h2><p id="protocol"></p><p><strong>Predeclared gate:</strong> at least 95% unit fill in at least 90% of selection seeds; then minimize mean modeled cost.</p><p class="small">This selection was written to disk before evaluation. Sensitivity results below never retrospectively change it. A service pass share is empirical, not a service guarantee.</p></section><label for="scenario">Operating scenario</label><select id="scenario"></select><p id="scenario-params" class="small"></p><div class="grid" id="cards" style="margin-top:22px"></div><section class="panel"><h2>Held-out service and cost</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Policy</th><th>Mean fill</th><th>Mean cost</th><th>95% cost interval</th><th>Seeds ≥ 95% fill</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table></div><p class="small">Percentile bootstrap intervals for means; paired candidate-minus-baseline intervals are in paired_comparisons.csv. Intervals are not adjusted for multiple comparisons and must not be treated as independent significance tests.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Policy sensitivity across scenarios</h2><label for="policyview">Diagnostic policy view</label><select id="policyview"></select><div id="chart" class="scroll"></div><p class="small">This diagnostic view does not change the frozen decision. Bars show mean unit fill. Amber line: 95% service target. Error bars: conditional 95% bootstrap interval for mean fill. Inspect per-seed service shares before making any operational recommendation.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Business interpretation</h2><ul><li>Forecast-aware replenishment may improve service under the base synthetic assumptions.</li><li>Budget restrictions can dominate forecasting differences. A failed service target should stop deployment, not be hidden.</li><li>Review frequency interacts with the daily non-carrying procurement allowance; changing it changes purchasing opportunities.</li><li>Lost-demand visibility, supplier variability, cost proxies, and real customer behavior require validation before a pilot.</li></ul><button id="download">Download scenario summary</button><details><summary>Declared experiment plan</summary><pre id="plan"></pre></details></section></main><script id="evidence" type="application/json">'''+data+'''</script><script>
const D=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('evidence').textContent),$=id=>document.getElementById(id),names={fixed_periodic:'Fixed periodic',rolling_mean:'Rolling mean',seasonal_buffer:'Seasonal + buffer'},money=x=>new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD',maximumFractionDigits:0}).format(x),scenarios=[...new Set(D.summary.map(r=>r.scenario))];
scenarios.forEach(s=>{let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=s;o.textContent=s.replaceAll('_',' ');$('scenario').append(o)});$('scenario').value='base';$('decision').textContent=D.selected?names[D.selected]:'No feasible policy selected';$('protocol').textContent=D.plan.selection_seeds.length+' independent selection seeds → frozen choice → '+D.plan.evaluation_seeds.length+' held-out seeds × '+scenarios.length+' predefined scenarios.';$('plan').textContent=JSON.stringify(D.plan,null,2);
function render(){let config=D.plan.scenarios.find(s=>s.name===$('scenario').value).config;$('scenario-params').textContent='Daily procurement allowance '+money(config.daily_budget_cents/100)+' · review '+config.review_days+' days · lead '+config.lead_days+'–'+(config.lead_days+2)+' days · shortage penalty '+money(config.shortage_cents/100)+'/unit · demand scale '+config.demand_scale;let rows=D.summary.filter(r=>r.scenario===$('scenario').value);$('cards').innerHTML=rows.map(r=>'<div class="card"><div class="tag">'+names[r.policy]+'</div><div class="big">'+(r.mean_fill===null?'N/A':(r.mean_fill*100).toFixed(1)+'%')+'</div><div class="small">mean fill · '+money(r.mean_cost)+' modeled cost</div><p>'+Math.round(r.share_meeting_95*r.n_seeds)+' / '+r.n_seeds+' seeds meet 95% fill · '+r.n_valid_fill+' valid / '+r.n_undefined_fill+' undefined</p></div>').join('');$('rows').innerHTML=rows.map(r=>'<tr><td>'+names[r.policy]+'</td><td>'+(r.mean_fill===null?'N/A':(r.mean_fill*100).toFixed(2)+'%')+'</td><td>'+money(r.mean_cost)+'</td><td>'+money(r.cost_lower)+'–'+money(r.cost_upper)+'</td><td>'+(r.share_meeting_95*100).toFixed(0)+'%</td></tr>').join('');}
Object.keys(names).forEach(p=>{let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=p;o.textContent=names[p];$('policyview').append(o)});$('policyview').value=D.selected||'seasonal_buffer';function drawChart(){let rs=D.summary.filter(r=>r.policy===$('policyview').value);let height=rs.length*42+45;$('chart').innerHTML='<svg viewBox="0 0 1050 '+height+'" role="img" aria-label="Diagnostic policy fill across scenarios">'+rs.map((r,i)=>{if(r.mean_fill===null)return '<text x="0" y="'+(33+i*42)+'" font-size="14">'+r.scenario+' — service undefined</text>';let y=18+i*42,x=200+r.mean_fill*780,lo=200+r.fill_lower*780,hi=200+r.fill_upper*780;return '<text x="0" y="'+(y+15)+'" font-size="14">'+r.scenario.replaceAll('_',' ')+'</text><rect x="200" y="'+y+'" height="22" width="'+(r.mean_fill*780)+'" fill="#167b73" opacity=".8"/><path d="M'+lo+' '+(y+11)+'H'+hi+'M'+lo+' '+(y+5)+'V'+(y+17)+'M'+hi+' '+(y+5)+'V'+(y+17)+'" stroke="#152a33" stroke-width="2"/><text x="990" y="'+(y+16)+'" font-size="13">'+(r.mean_fill*100).toFixed(1)+'%</text>'}).join('')+'<path d="M941 3V'+(height-30)+'" stroke="#bf8228" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 4"/><text x="200" y="'+(height-4)+'" font-size="12">0%</text><text x="945" y="'+(height-4)+'" font-size="12">100%</text></svg>'}
$('policyview').onchange=drawChart;drawChart();$('scenario').onchange=render;$('download').onclick=()=>{let keys=Object.keys(D.summary[0]),csv=[keys.join(','),...D.summary.map(r=>keys.map(k=>r[k]).join(','))].join('\\n'),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([csv],{type:'text/csv'}));a.download='simulated-robustness-summary.csv';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href),1000)};render();
</script></html>'''
